# Git commits

- Subject must start with `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, or `ci:`
- Keep it very short after the prefix (a few words)
- Examples: `feat: add telegram webhook`, `fix: deploy ssh quoting`, `chore: update deps`
- No long body unless the user asks
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:`, `Made-with:`, `Signed-off-by:`, or any Cursor/AI credit
- Do not pass git `--trailer` for Cursor attribution
